{"name": "Drone Chk'tu", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Born with an extra set of arms, drones are especially skilled with their hands.  Their hand-eye coordination and nearly doubled arm strength makes them exceptional builders, workers, and tenders.  Meanwhile, their four-armed approach to fighting makes them a force to reckoned with in battle.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;However, drones are born with stunted, useless wings if any at all, leaving them without any form of vertical movement.  This makes spotting a drone chk'tu far from its home or hive unlikely.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Drone Chk'tu Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Insectoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Strength increases by 2.</li><li><b>Trade Proficiency: </b>You are proficient in one Trade your choice.</li><li><b>Extra Arms: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.5QYD3QFDLZO2NKCD]{Extra Arms}</li><li><b>Multitasker: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.DSW72S4UGRPZ789H]{Multitasker}</li><li><b>Handsy: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.ND986T2ORMSDKFYJ]{Handsy}</li><li><b>Lifter: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.4F8FWF6AU6ZW5AWV]{Lifter}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "Q1W0MAQPZO74ZO48", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Royal Chk'tu", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Despite their name, Royal Chk'tu, are not inherently leaders or royalty.  However, their comparably extreme lifespan gives them a long-term perspective that others of their kind necessarily lack.  This makes them the natural pick for chk'tu leadership, almost always being the senior officer or eldest boss in any room of chk'tu.  Royal chk'tu's comparative rarity helps this, often having offspring of different branches before giving birth to another royal chk'tu.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;While not always the case, royal chk'tu are often put off by non-chk'tu.  Being used to the pampered and obedient treatment of other chk'tu makes interactions with those outside their hive seem disrespectful or brash.  On the other hand, some royal chk'tu, especially those with non-essential roles, tend to want external interactions, preferring the equal treatment they receive.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Royal Chk'tu Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Insectoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Wisdom and Presence each increase by 1.</li><li><b>Expanded Lifespan: </b>Royal chk'tu can live up to 50 years old. </li><li><b>Royal Piping: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.6LMVQ9ZOP41IHVCP]{Royal Piping}</li><li><b>Flutter Jump: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.3RN1CJEJ8YBYOC14]{Flutter Jump}</li><li><b>Flutter Fall: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.XQVA2ZE3HFJHJ8Z4]{Flutter Fall}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "VAHAFXTXKJMFUPA6", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Scout Chk'tu", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Scout chk'tu are slimmer chk'tu born with six wings instead of the usual four that warrior chk'tu are born with. A scout chk'tu's wings also come with a larger wingspan that allows them to fly without landing so long as the chk'tu has the energy to do so.  They also uniquely have a set of antennae that are highly sensitive to the scents of flora.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;These flying chk'tu are often given roles as scouts, foragers, and air support, as well as territory guards, messengers, and hunters.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Scout Chk'tu Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Insectoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Dexterity increases by 2.</li><li><b>Slow Walker: </b>Your base walking speed is 20ft instead. </li><li><b>Flight: </b>You have a flying speed of 25ft.  To use this speed, you cannot be wearing medium or heavy armor.</li><li><b>Olfactory Antennae: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.PX53DTW4FKMESH8I]{Olfactory Antennae}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "H552BBVLVMF536NB", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Warrior Chk'tu", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>To many not used to chk'tu hives, the warrior chk'tu are the variation that most stand out the most amongst a swarm.  Warrior chk'tu are covered in a more distinct, angular chitin exoskeleton, with a pair of bladed arms above a usual set.  A heavy swollen abdomen hangs almost to the floor beneath and behind the chk'tu, revealing a remarkably sharp regenerative sting when threatened.  To those who have survived war against chk'tu, the fast, fluttering, high-pitched movement of these bladed warrior chk'tu are horrors that they dare not to recall.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;To their allies, however, warrior chk'tu are often safe and caring protectors.  Their almost unnaturally safe control of their blades and stingers makes them shining knights to young chk'tu, and indeed to any ally with which a warrior chk'tu chooses to side.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Warrior Chk'tu Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Insectoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Strength and Constitution each increase by 1.</li><li><b>Natural Armor: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.2S9EWQFOXT06P29E]{Natural Armor}</li><li><b>Blade Arms: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.BX78MZPVZ495PPDG]{Blade Arms}</li><li><b>Death Sting: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.W2JOTIASQTIRW3IA]{Death Sting}</li><li><b>Flutter Jump: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.3RN1CJEJ8YBYOC14]{Flutter Jump}</li><li><b>Flutter Fall: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.XQVA2ZE3HFJHJ8Z4]{Flutter Fall}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6ERTR13JIVRUPXA3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Dark Elf", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>In the same way that night mirrors the day, Dark Elves are a mirror to Light Elves.  Dark Elves, too, have more powerful innate magic than Dusk and Dawn elves.  They were born powerful, gifted with magic, and their continued usage of their innate gifts have nurtured that power to continue to be passed down through their bloodlines.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dark Elves, however, do not see magic as just a tool or second nature.  Their heritage and magical natures are something that they embrace fully, and believe that it is their way to bettering themselves.  Magic is how they define themselves and express who they are to the world.  It is a power given to them to nurture and grow, and they put all of their faith and zeal into their magic.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Most Dark Elves have a standard height and weight for their race, but they are greatly differentiated by their colors.  Their skin is all shades of gray and black, with eyes that span most hues of red and violet, and occasional pairs of gold, silver, or amber.  Their hair stays within a spectrum of white, blond, and silver.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Dark Elf Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Wisdom increases by 1.</li><li><b>Skill Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in the Wisdom (Theology) skill.</li><li><b>Fey Ancestry: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.B6D7U0WZJRIXIX5O]{Fey Ancestry}</li><li><b>Darkvision: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.1F3VSNLQTVMYA4PE]{Darkvision (60ft)}</li><li><b>Cantrip: </b>You know one Cantrip of your choice from the cleric spell list.  You can use your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence as your spellcasting attribute for this spell.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "UMQ2LIKAJ3Q5UYIM", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Dawn Elf", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While elves may be magical in nature, not all of them hinge their lifestyles on it.  Dawn elves, while they accept their Fey heritage, find that it is not a central part of who they are.  The world is too vast to spend one\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s whole life focused on one\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s origins and ancestry, and they intend to prove that.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dawn elves do retain a few traces of their magical nature, but have left it to the wayside over the centuries.  It has dwindled in its intensity and left dawn elves to develop as a more physically powerful race.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;So instead of magic, dawn elves are built for exploring and traveling, having more endurance and a greater stride than Light and Dark Elves.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Compared to other elves, dawn elves are taller, slightly more muscular, and have sharper, more rugged features.  They find themselves more adept at moving around their environment and interacting with others rather than casting magic.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Their skin color ranges across the shades of bronze and copper tones, with darker reds and browns as well.  They have eyes of brown, green, and hazel, tending towards darker hues, and hair that comes commonly in the colors of black or shades of green.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Dawn Elf Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Presence increases by 1.</li><li><b>Skill Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in one skill from the following list: Arcana, Culture, Nature, or Theology.</li><li><b>Extra Language: </b>You can speak, read, and write one extra language of your choice.</li><li><b>Weapon Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in Quarterstaffs, Scimitars, and Longbows.</li><li><b>Navigator: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.OXY335G1JVFPRA6V]{Navigator}</li><li><b>Road Less Traveled: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.FLXLXLGUDQ22W74S]{Road Less Traveled}</li><li><b>Lesser Fey Ancestry: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.N3YTNUP9KU47ZSZV]{Lesser Fey Ancestry}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "Y2O2XJF9VIX3K9AR", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Dusk Elf", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Not all elves care for being a descendant of the Fey.  In fact, there are those that are trying to distance themselves as much as possible from said heritage.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dusk Elves, unlike their brethren, have almost no connection to their ancient ancestors or their Fey heritage.  They have taken a collective step to limit their spellcasting, causing their fey ancestry to dwindle over time to the point where it now has little to no effect on their physical beings.  There are, at times, some dusk elves that take up spellcasting, it is not a common practice.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Instead, dusk elves are valuers of hard work and put stock in what can be seen and can be done with your own two hands.  Actions speak louder than words to dusk elves, and, overtime, they have become physically separate from their brethren.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dusk elves are shorter than their counterparts, but stockier and physically bulkier as well, with more muscular forms than the stereotypical elf.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;They have skin colors of dark blues and violets, and hair colors of white, deep brown, silver, and blond.  Their eye colors are normally greens, blues, and darker browns, with occasional ambers.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Dusk Elf Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Strength increases by 1.</li><li><b>Weapon Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in Rapiers, Midswords, and Longbows.</li><li><b>Darkvision 30ft: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.K2R4176S4B99TO6R]{Darkvision (30ft)}</li><li><b>Unstoppable: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.LZ84NS4W5BKFFEI8]{Unstoppable}</li><li><b>Magic Means Nothing: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.B5HHGGP9E3Z81TY8]{Magic Means Nothing}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "4DRVDHD3H8WD22IS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Light Elf", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Most elves are considered to have some ancestral ties to the Fey.  Light Elves in particular, show this aspect off well.  These are elves that were gifted with more innate magic than others.  In fact, over the centuries that they have spent embracing this aspect of themselves, their connection to magic has only become stronger.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Light Elves use magic as though it were simply another limb; it is an extension of themselves, a muscle to be trained, and second nature to them.  They have a keen mind for the mastery and knowledge of the magical arts and for knowledge in general, making them seem like know-it-alls to others from time to time.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Physically, light elves are average in height and weight for their race, but their skin comes in lighter, more metallic colors, such as silver, gold, and alabaster.  Their eyes tend towards yellows, oranges, and gold, with hair colors of blonde, black, and brown being among the most common.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Light Elf Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Intelligence increases by 1.</li><li><b>Skill Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in the Intelligence (Arcana) skill.</li><li><b>Fey Ancestry: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.B6D7U0WZJRIXIX5O]{Fey Ancestry}</li><li><b>Illuminary: </b>You can cast the spell @Compendium[undertaking.spells-cantrips.NTGJ71IJ1VDA3GS9]{Luminescence} as a cantrip without needing to use the verbal or somatic components.</li><li><b>Cantrip: </b>You know one Cantrip of your choice from the wizard spell list.  You can use your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence as your spellcasting attribute for this spell.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "Y2O2XJF9VIX3K9AR", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Ba Huagin", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Aquatic (or Reptilian*)</p><p>Ba Huagin are diminutive, four-armed huagin with more vivid colorations, larger, more emotive eyes, and whiskered tendrils on a lizard-shaped head.</p><p>There are many rumors as to why ba huagin are so diminutive and almost draconic compared to others of their kind. While sometimes thought to be the result of a literal marriage of a huagin and kobold, the belief most often held by the huagin themselves is that ba huagin are descendents of huagin who worshiped sea dragons. The influence of these dragons twisting them over centuries into a shape more befitting the service of a dragon before some apocryphal splintering that made these huagin their own masters once more.</p><p>Either case it implies an ancestral connection to kobolds that often leaves ba huagin looked down upon by their kind, forcing some to work that much harder for approval. Other ba huagin embrace it, identifying as equally kobold as they are huagin.</p><p>That said, debates about their origins don&rsquo;t stop there. Some evidence points to ba huagin existing even before huagin, implying that huagin bred their desirable four-armed trait into their kind while breeding out perceived undesirable traits like smaller and weaker bodies, resulting in the much-respected saba huagin, whose name literally means &ldquo;huagin of the sa and ba.&rdquo; Though popular amongst ba huagin, this theory is rarely spoken about loudly by those without a death wish.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Ba Huagin Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Small Size:</strong> Your size is now Small. Your height decreases by about 1d4 feet, and your weight decreases by half of your core race&rsquo;s weight.</li><li><strong>Skill Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in the Intelligence (Arcana) skill.</li><li><strong>Increased Swim Speed:</strong> Your swim speed is increased by 15 feet.</li><li><strong>Sunlight Sensitivity:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.YQWX74CA8BA3ZKDG]{Sunlight Sensitivity}</li><li><strong>Dry Skin:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.8UMKZTEWXL5TOHF4]{Dry Skin}</li><li><strong>Extra Arms: </strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.YLHO6P1KHCUAL9OP]{Extra Arms}</li><li><strong>Four-Handed:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.60SP46N54DDHRTIR]{Four-Handed}</li><li><strong>Tri-Wield:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.5YTUEHPZ18OHVJ18]{Tri-Wield}</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Alternate Compatibility:</strong> This branch race can be mixed with a &ldquo;reptilian&rdquo; compatibility core race during character creation. If you do so, you also gain the following racial trait:</p><ul><li><strong>Reduced Swim Speed:</strong> Your swim speed is reduced by 15 feet.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "8O52WENNC1UTGRYC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sa Huagin", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Aquatic</p><p>The most common form of huagin, sa huagin are equally as dangerous and capable as their four-armed brethren. Not the least of which because of their sharp teeth, matched only by their even sharper killer instinct. Sa huagin are the top of the food chain in many parts of the sea, their bodies equipped with a hyper-reactive sense of smell and taste for blood. Their four-armed brethren&rsquo;s whirlwind of synchronized weapons are terrifying, but what originally earned huagin the land-term of &ldquo;sea devil&rdquo; came from the sa huagin&rsquo;s terrifying ability to dig into an opponent in battle, both in sea and on land.</p><p>That is a sa huagin from a land-dweller&rsquo;s perspective. To many sea dwellers, what they breathe is polluted by many undesirable elements from sea life alone, and underwater hunting only adds more to that. Fortunately for sa huagin, blood has a slightly tangy taste and smell&mdash;instead of metallic&mdash;that activates a hairtrigger shot of adrenaline in them when sensed. In a flash, a sa huagin can hone in and bite down on any target unlucky enough to bleed near them, should they want to.</p><p>Despite popular belief, sa huagin are not slaves to this instinct, however, nor do they find the taste of blood irresistible. While it can make rare meals particularly blood-pumping, blood is an otherwise intense firestarter for sa huagin just going about their day. It can be frustrating to deal with outside of life-or-death situations. Furthermore, if it's the blood of an ally or themselves, the flavor often turns sour.</p><p>Because of all of this, sa huagin culture tends to discourage bloodshed within their ranks. Even improperly treated wounds can be a trigger for nearby sa huagin and is greatly looked down upon. Where blood is to be expected or encouraged, however, such as combat arenas or meat markets, sa huagin are common, often working or enjoying such environments for the contact high. This brings us full circle; sa huagin are some of the first to prove themselves in combat&mdash;the benefits are undeniable.</p><p>Sa huagin may be notable for their hunter&rsquo;s instinct, but as one of the seas&rsquo; most widespread races, sa huagin are often seen in more mundane environments. The sea is a bountiful place, and many sa huagin are content with making a life in their slice of the ocean. Those who go on land, however, often find the environment inhospitable. More so than ba or saba huagin, sa huagin are less likely to be found on land willingly. However, sa huagin crowd their seas, so those who do venture onto land benefit from standing out amidst their neighbors. Those who do adventure often seek a unique path to call their own, no matter how rough the path.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Sa Huagin Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Strength increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in one of the following:<ul><li>Wisdom (Instinct)</li><li>Wisdom (Medicine)</li><li>The Artisan Trade</li><li>The Smithing Trade</li></ul></li><li><strong>Bite:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.SHZ8D3VSLPA7EC50]{Bite (Sa Huagin)}</li><li><strong>Hemovore:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.ZNHVD01ULNMS0M0W]{Hemovore}</li><li><strong>Sunlight Sensitivity:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.IZYTI3UCBFDKWEUU]{Sunlight Sensitivity}</li><li><strong>Dry Skin:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.NJAX0XZ39VVJ7XNE]{Dry Skin}</li><li><strong>Bloodsense 15ft:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.5X6VJGSD0ZYYKWDZ]{Bloodsense 15ft}</li><li><strong>Blood Frenzy:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.YVOL9DRHC1IM778U]{Blood Frenzy}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "9LNXNY4G4UR57EVK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Saba Huagin", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Aquatic</p><p>Saba huagin, whose name literally means &ldquo;huagin of the sa and ba,&rdquo; are four-armed, fish-like huagin. Unlike their brethren, however, saba huagin grow to be large creatures, as well as being terrifying four-armed multitaskers in and out of combat. Their size allows their four-armed styles to be even more terrifying, adding heavy-weapons into the weapons they&rsquo;re able to dual-wield. <br />Saba huagin, are born successfully less often, but when successful, many expectations get put upon them. While it&rsquo;s no guarantee that a saba huagin will be stronger than its brethren, saba huagin often have great expectations put upon them, as they usually attain high-ranking positions within their kind. While everything must be earned, combat is the most common way to earn it in huagin society, and few are willing to risk fighting a giant. Of those who are, even fewer can handle a saba huagin&rsquo;s four-armed onslaught, and the pressure of multiple attack angles often gets a surrender out of them before the fight truly begins. It&rsquo;s much the same in domestic life; saba huagin are desirable workers, often able to do twice the work in half the time.</p><p>Expectations are high, but what&rsquo;s not often said, is how much the saba huagin have to train to become so capable with their four arms. Unlike their ba brethren, saba huagin aren&rsquo;t naturally capable with all four arms, often colliding them during simple tasks in adolescence. Without proper practice, saba huagin may rely upon only one or two hands for tasks, losing their skill with all four in the process. This, paired with their size, often leads saba huagin to minimize their weapon variety to keep things in check. However, with their high potential, saba huagin tend to attract the best teachers to help them master themselves. A properly trained and fully grown saba huagin is more than just strong, they&rsquo;re the culmination of their kind&hellip; At least until someone proves otherwise.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Saba Huagin Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Strength increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Large Size:</strong> Your size is Large, taking up a 10sqft radius instead of a Medium creature&rsquo;s 5sqft. Your height increases by about 2+1d4 feet, and your weight increases by 1d4-1, minimum of 1, times 50% of your core race&rsquo;s weight. <br />For example, if you are a non-mixed Huagin, your weight might be around 1050-3000lbs at 9-14ft tall.</li><li><strong>Skill Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in the Intelligence (Arcana) skill.</li><li><strong>Sunlight Sensitivity:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.DRUBCSKJCK05ZOYF]{Sunlight Sensitivity}</li><li><strong>Dry Skin:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.2GAA77UD05M0NG97]{Dry Skin}</li><li><strong>Extra Arms: </strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.XW8D056N2NFMJA8J]{Extra Arms}</li><li><strong>Four-Handed:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.81XW5LGJ382S2UUE]{Four-Handed}</li><li><strong>Improved Dual-Wield:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.CWH17KUM5KF5QQSY]{Improved Dual-Wield}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "ARZCBPUK1VL3GBKC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Assimilant Human", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Humans are social creatures, drawn to others with whom they can socialize.  Humans build numerous cities for socialization, convenience, and dependency, but many grow even further past that.  Many cities form where humans live are deeply complex social and dependent hives of buildings and trades and gatherings.  Especially in larger cities, humans must balance a deeply complex and fast-moving social and economical environment, keeping on top of constantly changing luxury trends while the exponentially growing bills and social requirements keep them on their toes.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Assimilant Human Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Adopted Race: </b>Choose one race other than your core race.  You were adopted into this race's culture or have otherwise come to know the race as if you were one of their own.  As such, your knowledge of this race is comparable to a member of the race itself.</li><li><b>Adopted Attribute Increase: </b>Choose one of the attributes increased by your adopted race's core traits.  You increase that attribute by 1.</li><li><b>Adopted Language: </b>You can speak, read, and write one language listed under your adopted race.  If you already know all the languages of your adopted race, then choose one other language to know. </li><li><b>Adopted Weapon Proficiency: </b>You are proficient in the same weapons as your adopted race's core race.  Alternatively, you are proficient in the weapon proficiencies as one of your adopted race's branches.  If the adopted race has natural armor or natural weaponry, you can gain proficiency in all armors or unarmed attacks instead respectively.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the adopted race and its branches have no weapon proficiencies, then you are proficient in 2 weapons and 1 armor of your choice.</li><li><b>Behavioral Experience: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.IRC2M1N62DQTFVBH]{Behavioral Experience}</li><li><b>Cultural Osmosis: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.5WJE2EYK49R6V2YW]{Cultural Osmosis}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "UP1SP915S0SY961A", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "City Human", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Humans are social creatures, drawn to others with whom they can socialize.  Humans build numerous cities for socialization, convenience, and dependency, but many grow even further past that.  Many cities form where humans live are deeply complex social and dependent hives of buildings and trades and gatherings.  Especially in larger cities, humans must balance a deeply complex and fast-moving social and economical environment, keeping on top of constantly changing luxury trends while the exponentially growing bills and social requirements keep them on their toes.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>City Human Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Pick one attribute that you did not increase as part of your core racial traits.  Increase the chosen attribute by 1.</li><li><b>Skill Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in one skill from the following list: Culture, Insight, Persuasion, Deception.</li><li><b>Language: </b>You can speak, read, and write in one extra language of your choice. </li><li><b>Fast-Walker: </b>Your base ground speed is 35ft. </li><li><b>Night Owl: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.1G46RNQC5EFYGSXM]{Night Owl}</li><li><b>Hard Sell: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.AGC864XWZMAXOUFX]{Hard Sell}</li><li><b>Pocket Protector: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.I7IHUKZI8GA0BZ11]{Pocket Protector}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "N25WNWX5FZAOIQ1F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Country Human", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While humans are social creatures, many humans need little more than a village of people to fill that need.  Country humans were born into a lifestyle that felt no need for city luxuries or a fast-paced lifestyle.  Raised instead to focus on family, friends, and hard work, country humans have a different view on life.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Country Human Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Pick one attribute that you did not increase as part of your core racial traits.  Increase the chosen attribute by 1.</li><li><b>Skill Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in one skill from the following list: Athletics, Craft, Nature, Instinct.</li><li><b>Weapon Proficiency: </b>You have proficiency in sickles, scythes, tridents, and whips. </li><li><b>Farmer's Advantage: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.1GWNHHDFP2B30LUH]{Farmer's Advantage}</li><li><b>Pet Pal: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.BX9VETXWGYCFYBBD]{Pet Pal}</li><li><b>Early Bird: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.JQVEQW294G49HFD8]{Early Bird}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "CDYRKY4P7OPN6YV4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gifted Human", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Things come easy to gifted humans.  Humans, in general, are uniquely capable at most things, but gifted humans are often even more capable on average.  Be it through genes, luck, or divine intervention, gifted humans are a cut above the common folk, and are often picked on for this.  However, as with most gifts, those who rely upon their natural talent are quickly surpassed by those who work hard.  Gifted humans who really work at it, though, are capable of almost anything.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Gifted Human Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Hominoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Pick three <i>different</i> attributes that you did not increase as part of your core traits.  Increase each of these attributes by 1.</li><li><b>Skill Proficiency: </b>You learn one skill proficiency of your choice.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "7C21QRNJ9UNGWPO1", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bright-Hide Kobold", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Much like their strong-claw brethren, bright-hide kobolds help make up the majority of kobold society. While the shimmer-scales have the flashier scales, the color of the bright-hide kobolds scales are bolder, brighter, and more saturated. <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Bright-hide kobolds are proud of their scales as their claim to dragon ancestry. With thicker scales, resistance to the elements, and a hardier constitution than their kin, bright-hide kobolds work as builders, tunnelers, miners, and haulers within their society.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;They tend to carry a greater disdain towards wing-beat kobolds than the rest of their brethren though, as bright-hide kobolds believe they hold the strongest tie to their ancestors, not the wing-beat kobolds.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Bright-Hide Kobold Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Reptilian</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Constitution increases by 1.</li><li><b>Draconic Resilience: </b>You have resistance to the damage type associated with your draconic ancestry. The colors and their corresponding damage types are as follows:<br /><table><tr><th>Ancestry</th><th>Damage Type</th></tr><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></tbody></table></li><li><b>Tough Scales: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.6H6U8OS3L3B97ICX]{Tough Scales}</li><li><b>Elemental Spit: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.UVQHH4CUD3D9PVZR]{Elemental Spit}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "LLVIMHG55VS2VLEE", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Shimmer-Scale Kobold", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While not as rare as wings, shimmer-scale kobolds are still on the uncommon side of the population.  Their unique abilities tends to be fairly useful when it comes to blending in with their surroundings to sneak around danger or ambushing an invader.  This gift can also be used for fascinating others, looking more appealing, and presenting themselves as less threatening.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;These kobolds have more reflective and shinier scales than their counterparts and possess the ability to change both the color of their scales and how shiny their scales are to fit the needs of the situation at hand.  Their ability to blend in allows them to perform better in their duties by staying out of sight and luring enemies into a false sense of security.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Shimmer-scale kobolds normally find their speciality in things that either have them staying out of sight, or being the center of attention. There are even some that instead become diplomats of sorts, and act as representatives for their tribes when dealing with others.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Shimmer-Scale Kobold Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Reptilian</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Presence increases by 1.</li><li><b>Fascinating Colors: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.ZNZV2MPB10KLX45B]{Fascinating Colors}</li><li><b>Blending In: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.PK3LAXCYY6043RY5]{Blending In}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "27H8Q6WAYU8F0OMO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Strong-Claw Kobold", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Strong-claw kobolds are what makes up most of a kobold population, along with bright-hide kobolds.  Strong-claws are the workers, the warriors, and the laborers of kobold society and they play a crucial role in keeping their tribes safe.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;As their name suggests, these kobolds are born with powerful claws capable of being used as digging tools to make tunnels and deal lethal damage to enemies.  This makes them prime candidates for tunnelers, builders, and warriors of their tribes.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Physically, these kobolds' unique feature is their claws, which stand out as being larger, sharper, and don't wear down as fast as other kobolds' claws do.  While that may not seem like much to other races, among kobolds it is a thing of pride.  Because of their tendency to be warriors and builders, strong-claw kobolds tend to have a slightly keener mind for tactics than other kobolds.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Strong-Claw Kobold Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Reptilian</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Strength increases by 1.</li><li><b>Helping Hand: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.2H84NPVAS7007JRB]{Helping Hand}</li><li><b>Sharp Claws: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.1AW2E5YMMC1IGGP9]{Sharp Claws}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "NR2TN3OPH4LCBYZ3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Wing-Beat Kobold", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>While not considered wholly scarce, kobolds that are born with wings are rarer than any of their brethren.  They are hailed as having been gifted by their draconic ancestry, and are held in both awe and resentment in equal parts for this gift.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wing-beat kobolds share most physical traits with their kin, with the single exception of two large, leathery, dragon-like wings sprouting from their shoulder blades.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Within their own society, wing-beat kobolds tend to find themselves filling roles as scouts, perimeter guards, or hunter-gatherers.  Their access to flight, even if it is limited, gives them a great advantage when looking for possible dangers and allows them to get to places where others do not have access, which grants them the boon of expanded hunting grounds.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;However, more times than not most wing-beat kobolds work with other wing-beat kobolds.  This is to avoid any jealousies from their brethren while working.  Most kobolds with wings would rather work with others of their own unique breed or alone if they have a say in it.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Wing-Beat Kobold Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Reptilian</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Wisdom increases by 1.</li><li><b>Skill Proficiency: </b>Choose either Dexterity (Acrobatics) or Wisdom (Perception).</li><li><b>Lesser Flight: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.IX6N1K5PUGT3QCMV]{Lesser Flight}</li><li><b>Glide: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.8O5WZBNA6CHJTPSE]{Glide}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2VY82EAMZ8W3GIQ2", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Chthonic Lep'ix", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Insectoid</p><p>Chthonic Lep&rsquo;ix have an affinity for the realms of gloom and turmoil. Their mystical gifts portend ruin and obscuration. Their wing patterns tend toward darker or less saturated tones, sometimes complemented by striking high-contrast elements. These may form the shapes of uncanny visages, chaotic intersecting geometry, or sinister eyes, to name a few. Despite their infernal influence, a chthonic lep&rsquo;ix&rsquo;s powers and wing patterns don&rsquo;t tend to draw from a devil or demon&rsquo;s powers. Rather, drawing upon infernal realms themselves instead.</p><p>Despite these infernal associations and a naturally more gothic appearance, chthonic lep&rsquo;ix are still lep&rsquo;ix by nature, and not necessarily any more or less devious. Hard to convince outsiders of that, however, with chthonic lep&rsquo;ix trending toward being out at night where their eyes glow red. Indeed, many people's first sighting of a chthonic lep&rsquo;ix tends to be a pair of faint red eyes in the dark. The superstitious consider this a bad portent or sign of danger&mdash;akin to having a black cat cross one&rsquo;s path. These stories come from some amount of truth: chthonics have exceptionally great darkvision and are often out at night. So if one meets a lep&rsquo;ix in the night, it likely knows something they don&rsquo;t. Whether the lep&rsquo;ix approaches with a warning or a threat, however, is another thing.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<h4>Chthonic Lep'ix Traits</h4><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Dexterity and Presence both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Baleful Resistance:</strong> You have resistance to necrotic damage.</li><li><strong>Language:</strong> You can speak, read, and write Infernal.</li><li><strong>Darkvision 60ft:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.DY1RSHJ35NQJIMNJ]{Darkvision 60ft}</li><li><strong>Ominous Sight:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.2QNO86INI4E4DGTV]{Ominous Sight}</li><li><strong>Cryptic Essence:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.2M6GUTP8M5CJHMU5]{Cryptic Essence}</li><li><strong>Chthonic Magic:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.7P62CC0I70VY0V2J]{Chthonic Magic}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "YBDTRDD023A2IDS4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Elysian Lep'ix", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Insectoid</p><p>Elysian Lep&rsquo;ix have an affinity for the realms of idyll and divine grace. Their mystical gifts harken to the splendor and providence of an ideal world. Their wings tend toward a butterfly&rsquo;s wing shapes and patterns, and may develop breath-taking stained glass or metal embossed textures, representing symbolic or even prophetic designs. Despite drawing power from the divine, an elysian lep&rsquo;ix&rsquo;s powers and wing patterns don&rsquo;t necessarily draw from an existing divinity. Rather, a particularly devout or fate-bound lep&rsquo;ix might, but many elysian lep&rsquo;ix draw from the broader divine energies of elysium instead. This has led to suppositions that elysian lep&rsquo;ix are lesser divinities in their own right, such as a lesser deva or angel, or else a descendant of one. Any doctrine on the matter, however, is undercut by the fact that lep&rsquo;ix biology molds just as well to infernal or celestial magic as much as the divine.</p><p>When a lep&rsquo;ix comes of age and develops their magical connection, not only do their wings adapt to the change, but also their mind. A lep&rsquo;ix becoming elysian begins to carry themselves with an almost unnatural grace, and their speech patterns alter&mdash;their mind finding certain patterns and intonations of words more natural to say than before. Elysian Lep&rsquo;ix are truly sights to behold, and this often gives others pause who have not seen one before.</p><p>To lep&rsquo;ix cultures, elysian flare is less standout, and the differences between them is notable mostly like personality traits are. Elysian Lep&rsquo;ix communities are highly social, leaning on each other for the skills they lack, both verbally and physically. Others, however, seek out communities they can stand apart from&mdash;an elysian lep&rsquo;ix is less impressive in a crowd of their own.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<h4>Elysian Lep'ix Traits</h4><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Wisdom and Presence both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Empyrean Resistance:</strong> You have resistance to radiant damage.</li><li><strong>Language:</strong> You can speak, read, and write Celestial.</li><li><strong>Unmistakable Presence:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.26VHF3075B59HT0I]{Unmistakable Presence}</li><li><strong>Elysian Magic:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.LMZQYCB6DCLQ5XZL]{Elysian Magic}</li><li><strong>Healing Hands:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.7N0RHPPAXR3NO2WJ]{Healing Hands}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "XAWV9TOOU3YO4VE2", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sidereal Lep'ix", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Insectoid</p><p>Sidereal Lep&rsquo;ix have an affinity for the realm of stars and the celestial bodies that live there. Their mystical gifts are reminiscent of the grandeur of a starlit night and the pull of planets and moons as they dance above us. Wing patterns draw from the stars themselves, and may include features such as glittering constellations, colorful nebulas, representations of the sun or moon, or concentric and intersecting ellipses, to name a few. Their shifting wing patterns may even convey a slight glittering to onlookers.</p><p>Other lep&rsquo;ix are connected to long-proven sources of power&mdash;the infernal, tied to devils and demons, and the divine, tied to the celestials. Sidereal Lep&rsquo;ix, however, have a connection to that which was once thought to be indistinct from the divine, or else a stop-gap on the way to it that sourced only aberrations. The implications of sidereal lep&rsquo;ix continue to shake the magical world, implying further untapped and unknown powers beyond that of which are well established. This is also where some theorize lep&rsquo;ix are not originally from this world. The realm of stars is not well understood. The idea that fire lights the skies between distant rocks is not a well-known viewpoint, but by all accounts, sidereal lep&rsquo;ix are the origins of this rumor. Something within sidereals gives them an uncanny sense for the heavens; different parts, but often corroborated by others of their kind. Other lep&rsquo;ix don&rsquo;t have such a sense for it, but sidereals are said to be able to feel the space between stars in motion and are able to let it influence the world around them in a way that doesn&rsquo;t quite feel like traditional magic to a wizard.</p><p>Sidereal Lep&rsquo;ix are often seen as strange within their kind, less communicative in words as they are in feelings. Even in areas or societies that tend to create lep&rsquo;ix of a single type, sidereal lep&rsquo;ix are the most common unexpected magical bonding to have. These lep&rsquo;ix often get put in more magical or clerical work rather than social ones. Perhaps because of their outsider nature, sidereals tend to get along well with other races, lacking much of the intimidation factor of either other lep&rsquo;ix branches.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<h4>Sidereal Lep'ix Traits</h4><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Intelligence and Wisdom both increase by 1.</li><li><strong>Language:</strong> You can speak, read, and write Farspeak.</li><li><strong>Inner Orrery:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.TYJ1AYF7FU092BN0]{Inner Orrery}</li><li><strong>Twilight Messenger:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.BW9HAR7W7YO0Z9PH]{Twilight Messenger}</li><li><strong>Sidereal Magic:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.56ALYGLX05DJKFVC]{Sidereal Magic}</li><li><strong>Gravitational Interference:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.MSF5RJ7ZU7F16G1F]{Gravitational Interference}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "VHOSNZMN9WS2D4PJ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Bermecian", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>In many mecian cultures, military services is highly encouraged. In fact, these &ldquo;berm mecians&rdquo; are the most common mecian&mdash;berm standing for the simplest, and thus most reliable, form of something.</p><p>Traditionally, mecians are considered berm once they serve time protecting their people, or otherwise go through some form of formal combat training. Their skills are typically focused on the physical, and any standout birth talents, such as a geon or rego mecian&rsquo;s stronger telepathic capabilities, are lost due to lack of use or from being trained out of them.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Bermecian Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Increased Move Speed: </strong>Your movement speed is increased by +5ft.</li><li><strong>Weapon Proficiency:</strong> You have proficiency in either:<ul><li>Spears and all crossbows.</li><li>Two simple weapons of your choice.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Armor Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in Light Armor.</li><li><strong>Frost Walker:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.J5VT5KLFB5OS0TQV]{Frost Walker}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "U68CCQK54DD5A7QK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Cleymecian", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>In mecian etymology, &ldquo;cley-&rdquo; equally means &ldquo;without attribute&rdquo; and &ldquo;moldable.&rdquo; An apt title for those set apart from their people and forced to learn other capabilities as a result.</p><p>Born without the genetic ability to make psychic connections like their peers, cleymecians are social outcasts from their own kind. Not through lack of trying per say, they simply are neither fully able to understand nor communicate with their kind&mdash;a people so used to accenting their communication with emotive psychic signals that could never truly be translated into words. Not just that, their minds aren&rsquo;t built to receive psychics of any source, finding even the simplest psionic communication uncomfortable at best, painful at worst. The cherry on top; there&rsquo;s a connection between cleymecian parents and cleymecian children which has made relationships one all but taboo.</p><p>As a result, cleymecians must work extra hard to connect with their peers who quite simply think differently than they do. Through this life-long struggle, cleymecians are expert physical and verbal communicators, using every part of them to make up for their &lsquo;disability.&rsquo; Cleymecians have even developed a unique form of movement, or &lsquo;dance&rsquo; as some call it, to help translate meaning to others through sight rather than mind. It&rsquo;s considered so effective by some, that they believe a cleymecian&rsquo;s hypnotic movements have a psychic component to it in itself, whether subconsciously or not.</p><p>All of this makes cleymecians the only ones of their kind that connect easily with outside cultures, commonly ending up as diplomats and ambassadors as a result of their greater experience in what other races call &ldquo;traditional&rdquo; communication.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Cleymecian Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Presence increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Psychic Vulnerability:</strong> Your genetic lack of psionic capability further makes you less able to handle psionics in general. You are vulnerable to psychic damage.</li><li><strong>Skill Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in one of the following:</li><ul><li>Presence (Perform)</li><li>Presence (Persuasion)</li></ul><li><strong>Trade Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in the Entertainment Trade.</li><li><strong>Extra Language: </strong>You can speak, read, and write one additional language of your choice.</li><li><strong>Mystic Movement:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.JFC9GWTLDKMIWYI3]{Mystic Movement}</li><li><strong>Apsionic:</strong> If not a mixed-race, gain the following mecian core abilities:<ul><li><strong>Extra Language:</strong> You can speak, read, and write one additional language of your choice. <br />This replaces the mecian core ability &ldquo;Passive Reception.&rdquo;</li><li><strong>Incisors:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.4SO9XWEFMEM0T29Z]{Incisors}<br />This replaces the mecian core ability &ldquo;Touch Telepathy.&rdquo;</li></ul></li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "2F9AIZKEBDHRPTEB", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Geonmecian", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>&ldquo;Geon mecian&rdquo; quite literally means &ldquo;smart mecian,&rdquo; an apt term for mecians with a natural psionic talent. Geonmecians are considered great leaders and natural &lsquo;speakers,&rsquo; able to communicate and feel the feelings of others with little effort. As a result, geonmecians tend to be central members of mecian pods, or to succeed without one.</p><p>Their ability to convey and share emotion further helps them connect with those outside of their race, bridging the gap between their words and meaning.</p><p>In a world where they constantly catch glimpses of the unfiltered thoughts of those around them, and in a culture where the unsaid thoughts are as potent as those said, geonmecians are the most prepared to handle it all. With impressive mental fortitude, geonmecians often have an unshakeable confidence about the world around them. Within their own culture, success is all but guaranteed. Beyond that, they can rest easy in the knowledge that they are born with advantages that other races lack.</p><p>Geonmecians have the distinction of having much longer whiskers, thinner and more sensitive than those of their kin. They range between 1ft to 3ft long, and are just strong enough to stick out and wisp around, but not touch, the geonmecian&rsquo;s head when facing the wind or moving forward. A connection between longer whiskers and increased intelligence is an unproven wives tale. That doesn&rsquo;t stop mecians from aspiring to grow their whiskers longer as a result.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Geonmecian Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Intelligence increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Psychic Resistance:</strong> You are resistant to psychic damage.</li><li><strong>Empathic:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.Y19AYY7DSNR7VP8F]{Empathic}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "H64N3EQ0YXGJ7X1J", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Regomecian", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Like geons, &ldquo;rego mecians&rdquo; are unusually capable in psionics, but in an entirely different area. They don't just receive and transmit mental signals, they can also send neural signals into another&rsquo;s body with alarming potency, even to the point of being able to briefly control another. A simple nickname for this effect is where the term &ldquo;regomecian&rdquo; came from. The prefix being a simple conjugation meaning to act, or &ldquo;go,&rdquo; as the result of another&rsquo;s action; to be reactionary. As the one who causes another to &ldquo;re-go,&rdquo; regomecians was considered fitting when the term was coined.</p><p>Regardless, this capability is part of the cultural heritage of regomecians, tending to be fairly encouraged in their circles&mdash;within reason. Even amongst other mecians where the mind is considered less secret, it's considered extremely bad form to control another without permission. Fear and misunderstanding causes many to keep their distance from regomecians, and so they are often forced to hide their talents in order to fit in.</p><p>Unfortunately, while non-psionic races are unlikely to determine a regomecian&rsquo;s heritage, other mecians can immediately identify a regomecian through psionic touch alone&mdash;so strong is the mental force surrounding them.</p><p>Physically, regomecians have slightly shorter tails than most mecians. A connection between missing tail bones and increased psychic potency is theorized, but unproven.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Regomecian Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Presence increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Imposed Impulse:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.TMFEJKD6VESCN6XL]{Imposed Impulse}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "RI5EZE7T09OGJ0TK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Stramecian", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Str&amacr;mecians have built up particular dexterity in their tails, becoming able to use them in ways more numerous than most. This skill makes them expert multitaskers, though is culturally associated with shadier activities.</p><p>While it is possible to be born with a more flexible tail that trends one toward becoming a str&amacr;mecian, this trait is not genetic. It is, however, a skill that can be lost if not trained at a young age. It is also a skill often lost by str&amacr;mecians who go into service, where their more unique attributes get pushed down and normalized as part of training to be a berm. No wonder it&rsquo;s said that no str&amacr;mecian survives the army.</p><p>Adult mecians with such capabilities, regardless of their origins, are often called &ldquo;str&amacr;mecians,&rdquo; an insult that may be translated literally to &ldquo;street rat,&rdquo; referring to a common stereotype. However, using more cultural context, it translates closer to &ldquo;draft dodger,&rdquo; or simply &ldquo;space waster.&rdquo; Despite its nastier origins, the term stuck and is now casually used to refer more broadly to any mecian who breaks the mold, even as a compliment. <br />Despite a more controversial history in military roles, some str&amacr;mecians are hired or trained as specialists for their capabilities, even as assassins.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Str&amacr;mecian Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Skill Proficiency:</strong> You have proficiency in Dexterity (Sleight of Hand).</li><li><strong>Tail Requirement:</strong> If you do not have the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.0YU2TJMLJPZVTTPR]{Nimble Tail} trait from your Core Race, then gain that trait now. <br />In exchange, reduce your Strength attribute by 1.</li><li><strong>Tri-Wield:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.WRPRF15WQAE8RENU]{Tri-Wield}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "J9M67XIGBS2MIP9U", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Frost-Hide Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>With thick and shaggy fur camouflaged in whites and greys, frost-hide minotaurs are well adapted to life amidst snow and wind and ice. Beneath their coarse fur is an even thicker hide. Together, they trap heat extremely well and are exceptionally water retardant, running their blood hot even in the frigid cold. However their most effective body regulators are their horns. Often outward-facing, upturned crescents, frost-hide horns conduct heat in hotter weather, releasing excess into the air to keep their fur and hide from baking them from the inside out. Their hooves assist with this, relaxing muscles to let heat out of seams in their hooves when they grow too hot. Even with all of this, it&rsquo;s not uncommon for frost-hides to brush their fur in the mid-day sun in an attempt to let out excess heat and magical energies trapped between their fur and hide.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Frost-Hide Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Constitution score increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Cold Resistance:</strong> You have resistance to cold damage.</li><li><strong>Frost Walker:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.PO72QLL7HDNVWOUP]{Frost Walker}</li><li><strong>Tundra Heart:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.FTOHE443QKI6XBGG]{Tundra Heart}</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Alternate Heritage:</strong> Minotaur heritage can be present in various ways. If your core race does not already grant you Horns, you can choose to replace either the &ldquo;Cold Resistance&rdquo; or &ldquo;Tundra Heart&rdquo; racial traits with the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.HF5TGW1UQJY6J1GK]{Lesser Horns} alternate heritage trait from the start of this section.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "TG393M0WOPBA9YGC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mason-Mind Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Many gatherings of minotaurs lean rural, often nomadic or transhumant. Some of the oldest minotaur cultures, however, are more closed off and urban. Mason-Mind Minotaurs, unlike most minotaurs, have grown up in particularly urban or underground environments. These minotaurs tend to feel much more at home amidst the rigidly confining walls, corridors, and streets of a city, or tangled tunnels of caverns, than their nomadic kin.</p><p>While all minotaurs are born with a strong sense of direction, formative years spent navigating the various interconnecting interiors and exteriors that make up an urban sprawl or subterrain have honed an uncanny spatial sense.</p><p>In larger settlements where minotaurs, and thus mason-minds, make up a significant portion of the population, the spatial reasoning they bring to the table tends to have an emergent effect on the culture and even layout of their community. As the settlement grows and develops, it often becomes painfully obvious to resident mason-minds where shortcuts and more efficient routes could be created with minimal changes to foundation. Those who pick up masonry as either a profession or pastime, often find themselves in charge of their local infrastructure before long. Even those less inclined to stonework often find a use for their robust mental maps. Deliveries in settlements run by mason-minds are said to run like clockwork, and they are often sought after as couriers in cities abroad.</p><p>As changes are made to the layout of the city to facilitate new routes, older streets and passages become less used and are eventually bricked off so that their space can be reclaimed and used to expand the adjoining buildings. For this reason, cities where mason-mind minotaurs congregate tend to develop their own techniques around masonry and architecture that allow for quick construction and selective demolition without compromising on the stability of the structure. To outsiders who only occasionally visit these cities, however, the experience can be an uncanny one as the walls and streets seem to shift every visit. While for many minotaurs this ruthless pursuit of architectural iteration is a point of pride, it may also contribute to the stigma some hold which paints minotaurs as being obsessed with building mazes to some strange and unknown end.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Mason-Mind Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Intelligence score increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Trade Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in the Building or Pathfinding Trade.</li><li><strong>Architectural Intuition:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.7IE9OGRPT50ZUUAY]{Architectural Intuition}</li><li><strong>Spatial Reconstruction:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.76S5EYBF31K9S9L4]{Spatial Reconstruction}</li><li><strong>Bull in a Potion Shop:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.A3ZYWKJ6CPWV2VAL]{Bull in a Potion Shop}</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Alternate Heritage:</strong> Minotaur heritage can be present in various ways. If your core race does not already grant you Horns, you can choose to replace one of the &ldquo;Trade Proficiency\", \"Architectural Intuition&rdquo;, or &ldquo;Bull in a Potion Shop\" racial trait with the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.HF5TGW1UQJY6J1GK]{Lesser Horns} alternate heritage trait from the start of this section.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "VP2L0XDAYX49H9FO", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mountain-Horn Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Mountain-Horn minotaurs tend to thrive in some of the most rugged environments in the world. Steep terrain has honed their strength, and their horns have become fortified through contests with the local predators, giving these minotaurs their iconic name. They often feature powerful, spiked hooves and thick, ridged, curved horns. Their fur color varies but tends to be coarse, sometimes sun-bleached. Perhaps most distinct is the mountain-horn&rsquo;s bulk, especially on their upper halves. Built for climbing, with coarse and spined hooves and strong finger muscles, even weaker mountain-horns can lift their own weight up cliff faces with ease. This tends to carry to other feats of strength as well. Minotaur are sometimes called gentle giants, but those who say it haven&rsquo;t met an angered mountain-horn. As if the horns weren&rsquo;t enough, in the right, powerful hands, anything can be a weapon.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Mountain-Horn Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Strength score increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Climb Speed:</strong> With a strong grip and spined hooves, you find climbing and lifting your body surprisingly easy. <br />Your climbing speed is 30ft.</li><li><strong>Heavy Hitter:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.27PZP21ZBZM74HM9]{Heavy Hitter}</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Alternate Heritage:</strong> Minotaur heritage can be present in various ways. If your core race does not already grant you Horns, you can choose to replace either the &ldquo;Climb Speed&rdquo; racial trait with the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.HF5TGW1UQJY6J1GK]{Lesser Horns} alternate heritage trait from the start of this section.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "IM2OH22HF9MUJRHV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Valley-Hoof Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>When folks describe minotaurs, they often think first of their bull-like features, their formidable, almost top-heavy stature, and their horn. Valley-Hoof minotaurs are often what people envision. Found most often amid rolling hills and fertile valleys, valley-hooves are the most bovine of their kind, with large-nosed snouts on large heads, long horns, bent backs, and skin-tight pelts. Their stout build makes tough work like mining, hauling, and smithing look easy, and the abundance these boons bring make for a hale constitution. Their hooves are the toughest to crack and are uniquely flat, garnering them the misnomer &ldquo;flat-hoof&rdquo; minotaurs. This lets them distribute their weight across a larger area and across more lifting muscles, giving them more of a grip, even on mud.</p><p>Adding to the bovine comparisons, valley-hooves are generally thought of as docile minotaurs. Devious types sometimes mistake valley-hooves for pushovers and easy targets&mdash;a misconception short-lived after realizing a valley-hoof minotaur&rsquo;s reaction to provocation is as fearsome as any other.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Valley-Hoof Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Constitution score increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Increased Move Speed: </strong>Your movement speed is increased by +5ft.</li><li><strong>Runner&rsquo;s High:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.0FT24V5W1898J73O]{Runners High}</li><li><strong>Stamina Reserve:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.EKFZ9KVQTVVV81BU]{Stamina Reserve}</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Alternate Heritage: </strong>Minotaur heritage can be present in various ways. If your core race does not already grant you Horns, you can choose to replace either the &ldquo;Mighty Physique&rdquo; racial trait with the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.HF5TGW1UQJY6J1GK]{Lesser Horns} alternate heritage trait from the start of this section.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "UXQ9A2A606TN9K5V", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Wild-Blood Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Wild-Blood minotaurs share a kinship with the more primeval and remote stretches of the wilderness. They sport shorter horns and longer fur than most of their kin, sometimes with especially deep hunching, giving off a more ragged or natural look.</p><p>The wild-blood&rsquo;s tie to the natural energies of the world is rather unique, often seen with a lesser natural spirit in animal form at their side. While wild-bloods are able to conjure various animal forms, it is said that wild-bloods are soul-bound to the first spirit they ever conjure. This &lsquo;spirit guide&rsquo; is said to look over them through life and beyond from birth, and the summoning is just giving them a form. In fact, this initial animal form is said to become the easiest for the wild-blood to conjure from then on. Forming any other shape is thought to only re-shape their spirit guardian rather than call another. The cause of this connection is unknown, but being that wild-blood is generally hereditary unlike other minotaur branches, it&rsquo;s thought that these &lsquo;spirit guides&rsquo; may be the result of a bloodline blessing or are ancestral spirits looking after their kin.</p><p>Some wild-bloods also swear that they can understand their familiar, advising them either literally or indirectly. Perhaps a voice in the wind on their familiar&rsquo;s fur, or a tilt of the head that carries more meaning than it should, or even literal speech. In any case, it&rsquo;s often a source of reassurance and comfort for a wild-blood. It&rsquo;s for this reason that wild-bloods are thought to be wiser and more self-assured than their kin. Some wild-bloods are said to use their spirit guide&rsquo;s reassurances as an echo chamber that leads them to overconfidence and recklessness, others can&rsquo;t interpret their spirit at all, relying on their own instincts instead.</p><p>Regardless of the origin, wild-blood minotaur are most often connected and drawn to lush environments; forests, jungles, lakes, and marshes, for example.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Wild-Blood Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Wisdom score increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Spirit Guide:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.RZSLDAG5NL15FBEM]{Spirit Guide}</li><li><strong>Spirit Guidance:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.1THSTBQHCP5YUGKL]{Spirit Guidance}</li></ul><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Alternate Heritage:</strong> Minotaur heritage can be present in various ways. If your core race does not already grant you Horns, you can choose to replace either the &ldquo;Spirit Guidance&rdquo; racial trait with the @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.HF5TGW1UQJY6J1GK]{Lesser Horns} alternate heritage trait from the start of this section.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "3GAYY3A02QKOISF1", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Black-Crested Yarhuda", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Avian</p><p>Like all creatures, yarhuda have a primal survival instinct within them. Unlike most though, yarhuda have found a productive use for them. In combat, the psychological battle is as important as the physical one. As yarhuda warriors, black-crests have spent years training their mind to suppress and manage the psychological damage and instincts inherent in life-or-death situations through complex mental techniques. Taken further, black-crested yarhuda have developed a self-hypnotizing technique to mentally distance themselves from the combat, relying purely on instincts to pull them through. To their allies, they are brave and wise warriors trained in the mental tolls of struggle. To their enemies, they are dead-eyed, unreasoning terrors cutting across the battlefield.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Black-Crested Yarhuda Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Wisdom increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Calm Mind:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.WLAJ2YWVGZC2NL8Y]{Calm Mind}</li><li><strong>Battle Trance:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.0YDXA4M4W7KKFZM1]{Battle Trance}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "H40SEQE3WBAB004F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Long-Cloaked Yarhuda", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Avian</p><p>Yarhuda feathers, even their flight feathers, can vary in length depending on genetics. Long-Cloaked Yarhuda have naturally much longer plume feathers that hang down to their ankles while standing. Due to the weight and size of their feathers, extended flight is tougher and more unwieldy for these yarhuda. Instead, most long-cloaked yarhuda have spent time refining their control over their feathers, using them as weapons as well as producing blustering twisters that can serve to give them or others a lift.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Long-Cloaked Yarhuda Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Feather Cloak:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.K209GDHAKHLWD2ZO]{Feather Cloak}</li><li><strong>Storm Acclimatized:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.T3GAI02T73XXHXOT]{Storm Acclimatized}</li><li><strong>Flying Traits:</strong> If your core race has a flying speed, you have the following racial traits:</li><ul><li><strong>Additional Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Dexterity increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Short-Distance Flier:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.5Q2XHBBE46MGKS0R]{Short-Distance Flier}</li></ul><li><strong>Grounded Traits:</strong> If your core race doesn&rsquo;t have a flying speed, you have the following racial traits:<ul><li><strong>Reduced Move Speed: </strong>Your ground speed defined by your core race is reduced by 5 feet.</li><li><strong>Force Vulnerability:</strong> You are vulnerable to force damage.</li><li><strong>Feathered Furore:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.MWI5F41P3AGMTOBP]{Feathered Furore}</li></ul></li><li><strong>Wicked Wind:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.AE4EGB6H1CSLN85E]{Wicked Wind}</li><li><strong>Storm Starter:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.RR6BVPL9LOV2HAXV]{Storm Starter}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "3S3LUN8PSB0H1EJY", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Red-Billed Yarhuda", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Avian</p><p>Red-billed yarhuda, beyond just their red beaks, have particularly rigid and sharp feathers. They also have some of the loosest and fastest-growing feathers of any yarhuda, molting more often as a result. Using this to their advantage, cornered red-bills pluck their own feathers for use as weaponized darts, or kick up storms of molted feathers to slice into attackers. Feather plucking is a fairly painful proposition, but worth it in a pinch.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Red-Billed Yarhuda Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Constitution increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Weapon Proficiency:</strong> You have proficiency in Darts and Throwing Stars.</li><li><strong>Feather Dart:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.WHIWHF415AFOHZO3]{Feather Dart}</li><li><strong>Cutting Vortex:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.H7QEVR59YLDQIPH3]{Cutting Vortex}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "F6TEMJJHLQTKATEP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sharp-Shinned Yarhuda", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Avian</p><p>While all yarhuda have some form of natural talons, sharp-shinned yarhuda have talons of a much more intimidating size and curvature. While an obvious use for these claws are hunting and combat, sharp-shinned yarhuda tend to develop impressive finger control to match. Some use these skills to create, such as using their sharp talons and hardened hands for sculpting, whittling, and building. This increased hand dexterity has also spread to their arm feathers, allowing them some better control over them.</p><p>Sharp-Shinned Yarhuda are also some of the only yarhuda capable of wind dancing, which involves sharp-shinned holding colored dust under their feathers, releasing them during dances with swift movements to create vibrant wind-swept displays.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Sharp-Shinned Yarhuda Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Trade Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in one of the following:</li><ul><li>The Art Trade (Sculpting, Whittling)</li><li>The Building Trade</li><li>The Entertainment Trade</li></ul><li><strong>Reduced Flying Speed: </strong>Your flying speed defined by your core race is reduced by 5 feet.<ul><li>If you have a flying speed of 0, reduce your ground speed by 5 feet instead.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Bird of Prey:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.VHIDDMOZ69USKFHW]{Bird of Prey}</li><li><strong>Feather Pockets:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.CMXV21DFSWEDTHUC]{Feather Pockets}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "HVVXEQCPPMMDH7SP", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "White-Faced Yarhuda", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/birds/dove-pigeon-flying-white.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Avian</p><p><br />Unlike red-billed yarhuda, white-faces are actually not named for a naturally white face. Beaks in pales and whites are not entirely uncommon for yarhuda. Instead, white-faces are a term for a group of yarhuda trained in the sorceries and honorifics of death. The iconic white-faced yarhuda wears a white mask and beak paint with bleached feathers and accents of black and leather, their entire body being meant to appear like a corpse. Though more modern iterations have loosened this design due to its fearsome appearance, it remains popular amongst white-faces. <br />White-faced yarhuda are those who choose to more deeply study, understand, accept, and honor the dead as a next step to life. Realizing that only by mimicking and connecting to the powers of death do they better learn to respect the dead. <br />A common bedtime story for non-yarhuda is that white-faces are terrifying bringers of death for those who do wrong. While seemingly exaggerated due to the respect they earn within yarhuda communities, there is some truth to these stories. Due to the respect and power they have within their communities, when one does disrespect their dead, such as by grave robbing or resurrective necromancy, white-faces are sometimes called upon to put a stop to them. In either view point, a spurned white-face is a terror to behold.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>White-Faced Yarhuda Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Wisdom increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Reduced Move Speed: </strong>Your ground speed defined by your core race is reduced by 5 feet.</li><li><strong>Reduced Flying Speed: </strong>Your flying speed defined by your core race is reduced by 5 feet.</li><ul><li>If you have a flying speed of 0, then instead choose one spell listed in Corpse Casting. You are not able to cast that spell as part of the Corpse Casting racial trait.</li></ul><li><strong>Skill Proficiency: </strong>You have proficiency in one of the following:</li><ul><li>Intelligence (Culture)</li><li>Intelligence (Theology)</li></ul><li><strong>Corpse Casting:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.DSGZMV7CBP9IKHPD]{Corpse Casting}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "6YSHRIEYFM7P6PYK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Ether Zhier", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Born with a connection to the sky, ether zhier tend to have slightly longer and more airy fur and manes that flow when they move. Even on days when the winds are perfectly still, their thin, wispy fur seems to sway and dance in some unfelt breeze. It is said that ether zhier feel a kinship with the wind, and there are many who would trust it to carry their voice and even their very spirit across the land.</p><p>The sun and the moon and the earth are siblings of sorts. So the ether is that which flows between them, sharing within their orbits. The sign of ether represents connection, fluidity, and agility.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Ether Zhier Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Ethereal Jaunt:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.OFPN9HTKWIHFGJII]{Ethereal Jaunt}</li><li><strong>Voice on the Wind:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.9JN3KP9RXNJ1UWZJ]{Voice on the Wind}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "D03C9V0KHOLVXBLN", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Gaia Zhier", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Born with a connection to the earth, gaia zhier tend to have slightly sturdier-built bodies with keratin scales layered down their spine. With their natural control over themselves on land, they can curl into wheels and roll at high speeds without getting dizzy or losing track of where they&rsquo;re going.</p><p>The earth is the origin, home, and protector of the zhier. In many ways, zhier believe they owe gaia for its gists, and should protect it in return. The sign of gaia represents stability, growth, and physicality.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Gaia Zhier Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Constitution increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Armored Spine:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.7XEVJ8IGYPAM7913]{Armored Spine}</li><li><strong>Looped Locomotion:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.YW7J3KWFP497JP5P]{Looped Locomotion}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "V7WXGI4OHT3U4L14", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Lunar Zhier", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Born with a connection to the moon, lunar zhier tend to have smoother, flatter, and more reflective fur with less of a mane. Their connection to the moon manifests in their mind, with a feeling of confidence and capability in the moonlight. As they grow, this connection grows, giving them access to powers and knowledge of those older than them. Lunar zhier are known for having a mature understanding of their place in the universe that other species and zhier usually take much longer to grasp.</p><p>The moon keeps watch over the night, inspiring reflection upon and rest from the events of the day before it. The lunar sign symbolizes vigil, thoughtfulness, and change.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Lunar Zhier Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Wisdom increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Lunar Affinity:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.UEBZ9LPMH9YWUEKM]{Lunar Affinity}</li><li><strong>Lunar Cycle:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.6C0WDIXDL8N1AQSG]{Lunar Cycle}</li><li><strong>Nocturnal Light:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.5JTXJQ589XY9XY1R]{Nocturnal Light}</li><li><strong>Transient Magic:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.9YZ9MU6RHEEIME77]{Transient Magic}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "E4B9FHB3LRI32VVA", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Solar Zhier", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>Born with a connection to the sun, solar zhier tend to abound with energy. They often have brighter fur colors with larger tail tufts that more visibly spark with their birth element, should they have one. As they enter the fray of combat, striking an opponent, they seem to gain a burst of energy or adrenaline, spinning around for more strikes with shining speed.</p><p>The sun brings meaning, filling the days with happiness, and a trust that tomorrow will always come. The solar sign is warmth, energy, and emotion.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Solar Zhier Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Dexterity increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Resplendent Flail:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.5I4QJNLLGII5HT53]{Resplendent Flail}</li><li><strong>Solar Surge:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.SEVHM17XUDB3QKR1]{Solar Surge}</li><li><strong>Sunbathe:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking.abilities.NIR7W2U5N0DVWX8Z]{Sunbathe}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "UNKGD2I2DPBYCIXC", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
